⍝ D-96: an axis on a scalar function names the higher argument's axes the lower runs along
🍎> (3 5⍴1)+[1]⍳3
⍝ expect: 2 2 2 2 2
⍝ expect: 3 3 3 3 3
⍝ expect: 4 4 4 4 4
🍎> (3 5⍴1)+[2]⍳5
⍝ expect: 2 3 4 5 6
⍝ expect: 2 3 4 5 6
⍝ expect: 2 3 4 5 6
🍎> (⍳3)+[1]3 5⍴1
⍝ expect: 2 2 2 2 2
⍝ expect: 3 3 3 3 3
⍝ expect: 4 4 4 4 4
🍎> 0.3 0.2 0.1 +[1] 3 4⍴⍳12
⍝ expect: 1.3  2.3  3.3  4.3
⍝ expect: 5.2  6.2  7.2  8.2
⍝ expect: 9.1 10.1 11.1 12.1
🍎> ⍴(4 3 5⍴1)+[1 2] 4 3⍴⍳3
⍝ expect: 4 3 5
🍎> 2 3×[1]2 2⍴1
⍝ expect: 2 2
⍝ expect: 3 3
🍎> (3 5⍴1)+[3]⍳3
⍝ refuse: %axis-error
🍎> (3 5⍴1)+[1]⍳4
⍝ refuse: %length-error
🍎> (3 5⍴1)+[1 1]2 2⍴1
⍝ refuse: %axis-error
🍎> +/[1 2]2 2⍴1
⍝ refuse: %axis-error
